SCOPE NOTE — this repository contains material under three different terms.
The MIT grant above covers only the first.

1. CODE — MIT (the grant above)

   build.js, sw.js, and the HTML/CSS/JavaScript of the pages themselves.

2. ORIGINAL GUIDE TEXTS AND AUDIO — CC BY 4.0

   The section intros, work texts, "Look for" notes, the 2-hour route, the
   FAQ and the spoken introduction, written for this guide, and the recording
   of the spoken introduction (listen/before-the-prado.*), a synthetic
   narration made with Google Cloud Text-to-Speech. Reuse with attribution to
   this repository.

3. IMAGES — public domain

   The images in img/ (and the icons cut from Las Meninas) are faithful
   photographic reproductions of two-dimensional paintings whose authors died
   more than 70 years ago (the latest, Antonio Gisbert, in 1901). They were
   taken from Wikimedia Commons, where each file is marked public domain.
   Under Article 14 of the EU Directive 2019/790 on copyright in the Digital
   Single Market, transposed into Spanish law in 2021, material resulting from
   an act of reproduction of a public-domain work of visual art is not subject
   to copyright or related rights unless it is itself original. The image
   sources are listed in IMAGES.md.

This project is not affiliated with, or endorsed by, the Museo Nacional del
Prado. Corrections, and any rights concerns, are welcome as issues at
https://github.com/vicktorhugoqs/prado-guide/issues.
